  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "PutOffsets",
    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/array/concatenate.cc",
    "description": "When concatenating Binary/LargeBinary arrays (used by dictionary delta handling), PutOffsets computes values_range->length as `*src_end - src_begin[0]` without validating monotonic/non-decreasing offsets. For malformed IPC dictionary data, this can become negative. That negative range is later used by ConcatenateImpl::Visit(BinaryType) -> Buffers(2, value_ranges) -> SliceBuffer, producing buffers with negative `size()`, and finally ConcatenateBuffers calls memcpy with that negative size (seen as negative-size-param crash in buffer.cc:261). Crash site is ConcatenateBuffers/memcpy, but root cause is missing offset validation in PutOffsets during concatenation of untrusted data.",
    "conditions": "Fuzzed IPC stream provides a DictionaryBatch delta (`isDelta`) with a dictionary array of Binary/LargeBinary type whose offsets buffer is structurally valid enough to pass `dictionary->Validate()` but contains decreasing/inconsistent offsets. Data flow: stream_fuzz -> reader ReadDictionary -> DictionaryMemo::AddDictionaryDelta -> Concatenate -> ConcatenateImpl::Visit(BinaryType) -> PutOffsets computes negative value range -> ConcatenateBuffers memcpy with negative size. Trigger requires dictionary delta concatenation path and malformed binary offsets causing `last_offset < first_offset` for one concatenated chunk."
  },
